import Wikipedia.HopfProblem.PeriodFamilyHolomorphicCohomologyFourierEstimates

/-!
# Uniform Fourier-symbol input for genuine holomorphic period families

This module proves continuity of the original marked Dolbeault symbol in
operator norm, locally uniform positive real-frequency lower bounds, and
locally uniform nonzero integer-mode gaps.  The estimates are also uniform
on arbitrary compact subsets of the base.

The explicit Hermitian inverse formulas are jointly real smooth on the
nonzero-symbol locus.  Their original integer-mode specializations are
continuous in the genuine base parameter, satisfy the symbol equations with
the constant mode removed, and obey locally uniform order-minus-one bounds.
The scalar and top-degree formulas make no choice of a nonzero coordinate.

These are analytic inputs, not a claim of a derived base-change isomorphism,
smooth convergence of a parameter-dependent infinite Fourier series, or a
higher-direct-image calculation.
-/
